message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "A structural screen of the ESM Metagenomic Atlas for microbial drug-metabolising enzymes"
# ^ Title option 1 from the manuscript; change to your final chosen title.
type: software
authors:
  # Fill in the full author list before release.
  - given-names: "Mudasir"
    family-names: "Changal"
    email: "mudddy352@gmail.com"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # add if you have one
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mudddy352352/esm-atlas-screen"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a structural screen of the ESM Metagenomic Atlas with
  Foldseek, using ESMFold models of characterised bacterial drug-metabolising
  enzymes as queries, followed by an active-site-geometry filter, a Pfam
  profile comparison, body-site and nearest-relative inference, and docking of
  SN-38 glucuronide. The study prioritises metagenomic proteins within families
  that annotation already identifies rather than discovering new enzymes.
keywords:
  - pharmacomicrobiomics
  - metagenomics
  - protein structure prediction
  - Foldseek
  - remote homology
  - glycoside hydrolase family 2
  - cytidine deaminase
